investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"- GPUIL operates across four verticals - Energy (thermal, hydro, solar, wind), Smart Metering (AMI), Transportation & Urban Infra (highways, EPC, Krishnagiri SIR) and Smart Mobility (EV charging) - and is pivoting under a 'GPUIL 2.0' strategy from conventional energy toward smart metering, renewables and EV/smart-mobility adjacencies.\n- Management cites nearly three decades of presence across power-generation sources, in-house project management/O&M/policy-advocacy capability, over a decade of energy-trading experience, and GMR Group synergies (airports as fleet-owner/cab-aggregator hubs) as the basis for the GPUIL 2.0 transition.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Litigation] NHAI has filed a Special Leave Petition in the Supreme Court challenging the Delhi High Court order referring the Ambala-Chandigarh toll dispute to de-novo arbitration; arbitration awaits the SLP outcome.\n- [Litigation] The DFC Eastern Corridor EPC prolongation claim totals INR2,829cr, of which only INR506cr was considered as of 30-Jun-26.\n- [Receivables] Overdue accounted receivables of ~INR6.8bn (Energy ~INR1.8bn, DFCC ~INR5.0bn), excluding claims under litigation.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 14-08-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"GPUIL positions itself as a diversified energy-to-urban-infrastructure platform transitioning from conventional power generation toward smart metering, renewables and smart-mobility adjacencies under its 'GPUIL 2.0' strategy, while steadily deleveraging.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":-4.81,"fy":"FY22","mcap":2028,"opm":16.5,"pe":null,"roe":0.0},{"de":-3.13,"fy":"FY23","mcap":963,"opm":14.3,"pe":0.8,"roe":0.0},{"de":-4.75,"fy":"FY24","mcap":2586,"opm":31.5,"pe":null,"roe":0.0},{"de":17.44,"fy":"FY25","mcap":8173,"opm":34.4,"pe":